{"id": "EUVD-2026-102270", "enisaUuid": "c64d9d2b-1e09-370b-a33c-0c65a51d6042", "description": "Ansilove libansilove through 1.4.2 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in ansilove_xbin() in src/loaders/xbin.c that lacks bounds checks for compressed run-length records. Attackers can supply a crafted compressed XBIN file ending in a control byte such as 0x7F to read past the input buffer, crashing applications that render untrusted XBIN art.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:44:00", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libansilove-xbin-rle-oob-read-and-null-font-deref", "https://github.com/ansilove/libansilove/blob/f1b05447aa566aa4eef9b05ebf8c2aaf1e379cd3/src/loaders/xbin.c#L169-L241", "https://github.com/ansilove/libansilove", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ansilove-libansilove-through-1.4.2-out-of-bounds-read-via-ansilove-xbin-rle-decoding"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8q5r-4q94-f6qr", "CVE-2026-111143"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "bff38a1c-ef72-3d7c-986c-e9ce8c3514ce", "product": {"name": "libansilove", "vendor": {"name": "ansilove"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.4.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "298ad55d-9801-3ea1-aab8-1ff47e931bcc", "vendor": {"name": "ansilove"}}], "isExploited": false}